From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:13:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mesa/glthread: hand back no buffer when the driver refuses
 the upload

glthread copies the data of a glBufferSubData, and of a draw's client
indices and vertex arrays, into a 1 MiB upload buffer that the driver
allocates once and the calls share. _mesa_glthread_upload() assumed the
allocation succeeds and added the references it hands out in advance to
the buffer it got. A driver with a bounded memory budget refuses the
allocation once the budget is full, the buffer is NULL, and the host
faulted on the thread that runs the context's transfers, right after the
driver reported that it could not allocate memory.

The separate buffer for an upload larger than the shared one already
returns no buffer when the driver refuses, and every caller handles
that: a draw whose indices or vertices need the upload raises
GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY and is dropped, as a driver that cannot get memory for
a draw reports, and glBufferSubData falls back to copying its data into
the command stream, which needs no upload buffer. The shared path now
returns the same way. It took no reference, and the release before it
left the private reference count at zero, so the next upload starts
clean and asks the driver again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mesa/main/glthread_bufferobj.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/glthread_bufferobj.c b/src/mesa/main/glthread_bufferobj.c
index 09b0fbebbbcceebc3d5d629433222cb7a45e3bc4..6aab79a905c544af43ae0dee25871672b65087a2 100644
--- a/src/mesa/main/glthread_bufferobj.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/glthread_bufferobj.c
@@ -134,6 +134,16 @@ _mesa_glthread_upload(struct gl_context *ctx, const void *data,
       glthread->upload_offset = 0;
       offset = start_offset;
 
+      /* A driver with a bounded memory budget refuses the buffer once the
+       * budget is full. Hand the caller no buffer, as the separate-buffer
+       * path above does: every caller then takes its synchronous path or
+       * raises GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY. No reference was taken, and the release above
+       * reset upload_buffer_private_refcount, so the next upload starts from
+       * a clean state and asks the driver again.
+       */
+      if (unlikely(!glthread->upload_buffer))
+         return;
+
       /* Since atomic operations are very very slow when 2 threads are not
        * sharing one L3 cache (which can happen on AMD Zen), prevent using
        * atomics as follows:
